    {
      "object_id": "mathia_interpretation_feabe8b8829a54f5c907ba75ea7c5c1c315406c5041e8ca08ac5a9419196e334",
      "object_role": "interpretation",
      "proposed_content": "Tracing the semiclassical Green function filters path space by scale and stationarity: short local returns give the Thomas-Fermi mean, whereas long traced paths survive stationary phase only when initial and final position and momentum coincide, selecting isolated periodic orbits. Monodromy then measures transverse stability in each orbit's weight, but the formula assumes unstable periodic orbits, is semiclassical, and supplies neither convergence control nor exact spectral reconstruction.",
