    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_2bd3fdadc04efa5db7dfdac576bac1add54d74d7bd88b6332244b792a569d5ec",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "Diagonal equal-action pairing determines only the diagonal or smooth component and is generally insufficient for the full long-range correlation. In the zeta and modular arithmetic examples, the missing information is recast as correlations of nearby prime-power weights or nearby trace-length multiplicities, and rational-point singularities of generating functions convert arithmetic-progression means into the needed correlation terms.",
