    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_447b711912391d303cda5f28e83e1f84605e08bfad406f56f58fa3c5777f4d0c",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "The source identifies one half as a critical multiplicity exponent inside its diagonal semiclassical model: arithmetic mean multiplicity scales as e^(L/2)/L and can raise the form factor to order one before diagonal resolution fails, whereas an assumed e^(λL)/L law with λ<1/2 leaves the maximal diagonal contribution vanishing as energy grows, so exponential degeneracy alone need not contradict GOE statistics.",
