    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_54aebc6bd5b3ca6b2db71c48de137b1dbeac5468f760bd6b0c44b7caa995b33f",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "The source realizes a common spectral-to-dual-data architecture in several genuinely different regimes: an exact Poisson/group-sum identity for a periodic rectangle, a test-function Selberg identity for a hyperbolic quotient, semiclassical stationary-phase formulas organized by integrable orbit families or isolated unstable chaotic orbits, and the Weil explicit formula relating zeta zeros to prime powers.",
