    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_fdb2a273203a1920fd01702844ae3e015944ffefeec07b532a061b08af41246f",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "Arithmeticity constrains nonidentity embeddings of traces, making the admissible trace set grow only linearly while periodic geodesics proliferate exponentially; the resulting exponential fibers of the trace-to-length map create exact phase coincidences that amplify the diagonal form factor. The modular calculation then shows a smoothed Poisson limit, while a commuting Hecke algebra coexists as a separate arithmetic structure rather than a proved equivalent cause.",
